   * This operation initiates the password reset process for a user, conforming
   * to the system's policy for secure account recovery. The endpoint receives
   * an email address and, if it matches an entry in 'todo_users', sends a
   * one-time password reset token to that address. The email field is validated
   * for format and referenced via the unique constraint on 'todo_users.email'.
   *
   * No information about account existence is disclosed in the response, and
   * failure scenarios are handled generically. The password reset token is
   * time-limited, typically valid for 15–30 minutes, and is stored only in a
   * system-maintained context, never in the user table. Business logic for
   * actual password reset is handled separately via token consumption. The
   * operation is required for users who've lost their password or cannot access
   * their account using normal credentials.
   *
   * This endpoint is only accessible to non-authenticated users—those who need
   * to recover access. Limits on request frequency should be applied to prevent
   * abuse but are outside schema scope.
   *
   * Related operations: password reset document redemption (not shown),
   * login/join, session refresh. Security logging and rate limiting are
   * implied.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Registered email for password reset initiation. No other
   *   fields.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
